WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.079 --> 00:00:16.121
was quiet on the way to summer camp.

2
00:00:16.161 --> 00:00:19.422
"Don't be sad yet," said her mom.

3
00:00:19.442 --> 00:00:22.804
"You still have eight more hours of camp to enjoy.

4
00:00:22.824 --> 00:00:27.967
Go have fun, honey.

5
00:00:28.827 --> 00:00:35.289
Please!" On the blacktop Mr.

6
00:00:35.329 --> 00:00:39.030
Dunn was taping a large, square piece of mural paper to the ground.

7
00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:42.312
"Nina!" Ethan whispered loudly.

8
00:00:43.332 --> 00:00:46.033
He grabbed her arm and pulled her to the picnic table.

9
00:00:46.053 --> 00:00:48.154
"You have to sign Mr.

10
00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:48.974
Dunn's card."

11
00:00:56.538 --> 00:00:57.978
you bring the watering can?"

12
00:00:58.398 --> 00:00:58.999
she asked.

13
00:00:59.019 --> 00:01:01.780
"Yep." Ethan giggled.

14
00:01:02.924 --> 00:01:04.805
"Izzie hid it in the girls' bathroom!"

15
00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:06.405
"All right.

16
00:01:07.285 --> 00:01:10.166
Time to start our final project," Mr.

17
00:01:10.206 --> 00:01:10.906
Dunn called.

18
00:01:17.308 --> 00:01:18.528
we're making a quilt.

19
00:01:19.709 --> 00:01:24.050
It's like a quilt made of fabric, but ours will be made of paper.

20
00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:26.931
Everyone will design a square.

21
00:01:27.931 --> 00:01:30.972
Your square should show your favorite camp memory.

22
00:01:32.316 --> 00:01:35.858
But we're not really drawing our memories," Mr.

23
00:01:35.899 --> 00:01:36.539
Dunn said.

24
00:01:36.559 --> 00:01:42.083
"We're—" "Cutting paper!"

25
00:01:42.563 --> 00:01:43.343
Izzie cried.

26
00:01:43.363 --> 00:01:45.165
"Right, Izzie!"

27
00:01:45.585 --> 00:01:46.225
said Mr.

28
00:01:46.245 --> 00:01:52.149
Dunn. "We're going to cut shapes out of paper and glue them in our squares."

29
00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:55.872
They all headed to the picnic table to work.

30
00:02:00.888 --> 00:02:02.590
"What memory are you going to pick?"

31
00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:04.251
Izzie asked Nina.

32
00:02:05.332 --> 00:02:06.453
Nina sighed.

33
00:02:06.473 --> 00:02:07.814
"I don't know.

34
00:02:07.834 --> 00:02:10.617
I liked every day of camp!"

35
00:02:10.637 --> 00:02:15.401
"I'm picking the day we visited the animal shelter," Jason said.

36
00:02:15.421 --> 00:02:18.343
"And I got to see Lucy."

37
00:02:18.363 --> 00:02:23.247
"I want to pick the three-legged races.

38
00:02:24.268 --> 00:02:27.191
But that's going to be hard to show with paper shapes!"

39
00:02:27.631 --> 00:02:28.492
Bobby groaned.

40
00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:32.502
Izzie looked at Ethan's friendship bracelet and smiled.

41
00:02:32.522 --> 00:02:35.104
"I know what I'm going to choose."

42
00:02:35.124 --> 00:02:37.926
"What about you, Ethan?"

43
00:02:38.286 --> 00:02:39.107
Nina asked.

44
00:02:39.127 --> 00:02:43.510
"I liked when we made kites and flew them at the park," he said.

45
00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.491
"Okay, campers.

46
00:02:46.872 --> 00:02:50.114
Design your square in pencil first," Mr.

47
00:02:50.154 --> 00:02:50.795
Dunn said.

48
00:02:50.815 --> 00:02:54.037
"Then decide what color paper you need.

49
00:02:55.578 --> 00:02:57.579
If you're making a tree," Mr.

50
00:02:57.619 --> 00:03:01.614
Dunn went on, "you'll probably need brown paper for the trunk."

51
00:03:01.634 --> 00:03:05.996
"And green paper for the leaves," added Ethan.

52
00:03:06.016 --> 00:03:08.537
"Yep," said Mr.

53
00:03:08.597 --> 00:03:12.039
Dunn. "Does everyone understand what to do?"

54
00:03:16.081 --> 00:03:19.603
Nina understood how to cut the shapes and glue them on her square.

55
00:03:20.624 --> 00:03:22.825
She just couldn't choose the best day at camp.

56
00:03:23.925 --> 00:03:25.346
Was it when they made jam?

57
00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:28.248
Or the sea-breeze wind chimes?

58
00:03:29.596 --> 00:03:31.178
She watched her friends working.

59
00:03:33.359 --> 00:03:34.881
At last she got an idea.

60
00:03:39.525 --> 00:03:41.786
Everyone quietly cut and glued paper.

61
00:03:43.368 --> 00:03:45.129
Before they knew it, they were done.

62
00:03:45.149 --> 00:03:49.773
"Now let's put our squares together on the mural paper!"

63
00:03:50.154 --> 00:03:50.774
said Mr.

64
00:03:50.814 --> 00:03:53.937
Dunn. "We'll arrange them in time order."

65
00:03:53.957 --> 00:03:57.520
"Oh my gosh, Nina!"

66
00:03:57.896 --> 00:03:59.938
Izzie gasped when she saw Nina's.

67
00:03:59.958 --> 00:04:03.320
"Nina, that's beautiful!"

68
00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:04.941
Mr. Dunn exclaimed.

69
00:04:06.042 --> 00:04:11.425
Nina had carefully cut out tiny people working on even tinier colorful quilt squares.

70
00:04:12.986 --> 00:04:15.608
"I like yours too," Nina told Mr.

71
00:04:15.648 --> 00:04:20.952
Dunn. His square showed the water balloon toss from the first day of camp.

72
00:04:20.972 --> 00:04:24.894
"That's when I first met you guys."

73
00:04:25.775 --> 00:04:27.016
Mr. Dunn smiled.

74
00:04:28.064 --> 00:04:30.225
"Definitely the best day of the summer."

75
00:04:33.626 --> 00:04:36.906
At the end of the day, all the parents admired the quilt.

76
00:04:42.908 --> 00:04:43.928
The kids gave Mr.

77
00:04:43.968 --> 00:04:46.029
Dunn his card and the watering can.

78
00:04:47.289 --> 00:04:48.269
Everyone thought Mr.

79
00:04:48.329 --> 00:04:49.610
Dunn looked a little teary.

80
00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:53.451
"Were you okay today, honey?"

81
00:04:53.831 --> 00:04:54.951
Nina's mom asked.

82
00:04:56.091 --> 00:04:57.612
Nina pointed at her square.
